cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Explicit Hamiltonian ball packings in every dimension"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/s-JoL/Symplectic-Ball-Packing"
authors:
  - family-names: Song
    given-names: Liang
    email: sl12160010@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  For every k ≥ 10 and ε in (0,1), we define one explicit smooth compactly supported Hamiltonian on
  R × R^4 whose time-one map carries the k closed unit balls centred at (3i−3,0,0,0) into the
  ball of radius (k/(1−ε/4))^{1/4}, with an explicit stability margin. The same construction
  realises every ball packing allowed by the volume and two-ball inequalities in dimension
  2n ≥ 6, and every packing with Σc_i² < C² and 3c_i < C in dimension four, proving Biran's
  full-packing theorem for k ≥ 9 equal balls without J-holomorphic curves or Seiberg–Witten theory.
  Includes four papers (equal balls in the four-ball, general capacities and higher dimensions
  with a uniform finite-output algorithm, elementary packings and their obstructions, and
  closed-form C^4 equal-ball embeddings), supplements, a Lean 4 formalisation of the main packing,
  stability and algorithm theorems of Papers I–II, and two PyTorch programs (an elementary-flow
  generator for Epoch's ODE interface and a modular closed-form C^4 embedding evaluator for all
  k ≥ 10 and ε in (0,1) with arbitrary-precision verification).
keywords:
  - symplectic ball packing
  - Hamiltonian dynamics
  - packing stability
  - explicit constructions
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
